    },
    "message": "test: assert no FCC background thread survives a test session\n\nThe request-log and web-search stores each start a daemon writer thread. A\nstore that a test constructs and never closes keeps its queue, sqlite\nconnection and held records alive for the rest of the process; under xdist\nthat accumulates per-worker and reads as a memory leak with workers that\n\"won't die\". Daemon threads cannot stop interpreter exit, but the store they\nbelong to can pin real memory and hold an open connection indefinitely.\n\nAdd a session-scoped autouse fixture that resets both shared-store registries\nbefore and after the whole run, then fails loudly if any FCC-owned writer\nthread (request-log, web-search, oauth callback, admin-browser opener) is\nstill alive. Proven to catch the leak: a direct-construction WebSearchLogStore\nleft unclosed makes the session teardown fail with\n`assert not ['websearch-log-writer']`. Full suite: 3704 passed, 26 known\nenvironmental failures, zero leaked threads, zero leftover processes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
